  "slug": "networks-interactions-98aa",
  "summary": "Simulators, forecasters, and kinetic models are being used to infer how viral genotype maps to phenotype under immune and drug pressure.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is inferring how genetic sequence maps to phenotype when selection acts on it. antigen-prime is a forward-time simulator that links influenza genotype to antigenic phenotype under host immune selection and is used to benchmark variant assignment. The HIV protease forecasting study addresses drug-resistant evolution under protease inhibitor pressure. A third study couples AlphaFold2 ensembles, built at varying MSA depths, to a coarse-grained Langevin model to estimate conformational time scales across HIV-1 protease variants. These studies answer different questions with different models, so the common element is methodological. What is new is the focus on the mapping itself, pursued through simulation, forecasting, and kinetic estimation as alternative routes to the same target.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-31"
}
